#. type: Title #
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Work with bosonic circuits {#work-with-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") expresses a computation directly "
"on **bosonic modes**. It carries no truncation, no encoding, and no qubit "
"count: those enter later, during transpilation, which is how one circuit can"
" be lowered under several encodings and several truncations without being "
"rebuilt.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It deliberately exposes a reduced API compared to Qiskit’s "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit),"
" so that qubit gates cannot be applied to a bosonic mode, which would not be"
" a well-defined operation. This guide covers the operations that *are* "
"exposed for assembling larger circuits out of smaller ones.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Why use bosonic circuits {#why-use-bosonic-circuits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the traditional workflow for putting the time evolution of a "
"bosonic Hamiltonian onto a qubit-based architecture:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Define the bosonic Hamiltonian, for example $H = -\\sum_{ij} b^\\dagger_i "
"b_j$.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Choose a truncation and an encoding, and map the Hamiltonian to a qubit "
"operator with them.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Implement the time evolution in qubit space, by Trotterization or another "
"method.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second step comes early, and it makes two decisions that are expensive "
"to take back. The truncation fixes how many levels each mode keeps, and the "
"encoding fixes how many qubits that costs, so both are fixed in the qubit "
"operator before anything else has been done with the circuit. To look at the"
" same physics under another cutoff or another encoding, you map the "
"Hamiltonian again and build the circuit again. What the mapping discards, as"
" well, is the bosonic structure: which terms belong together, and that the "
"terms of a hopping pair are each other’s adjoint.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") moves those decisions to the "
"end:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Define the bosonic Hamiltonian.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Express the time evolution directly on bosonic modes, with bosonic gates.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choose the truncation and the encoding as part of the transpilation.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The circuit describes *what* computation to perform, and transpilation "
"decides *how* to put it on qubits. The same circuit is then lowered at every"
" cutoff and under every encoding, and the grouping of the operator is still "
"there for the passes that can use it. The next sections show how such a "
"circuit is assembled; [Transpile bosonic "
"circuits](transpilation#transpilation-explanation) shows it being lowered.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Generic mode indexing {#generic-mode-indexing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The [`operators`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/operators#module-qiskit_bosons.operators \"qiskit_bosons.operators\")"
" module and the circuit share one convention for modes. A mode is only an "
"index that labels a bosonic degree of freedom, and it carries no meaning of "
"its own. You can therefore evolve any operator that implements the "
"[`OperatorTrait`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/operators-"
"operator-trait#qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait "
"\"qiskit_bosons.operators.OperatorTrait\") protocol, whatever it represents,"
" and the circuit never needs to know what mode `2` stands for. The same "
"holds for the size of a mode: a circuit has no occupation cutoff, so nothing"
" here says how many levels a mode has.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Append gates {#append-gates}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Gates are appended onto modes. Only "
"[`BosonicGate`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-gate#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicGate\") instances are accepted:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Anything else is refused, and the error names the offending type:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Compose circuits {#compose-circuits}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`compose()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.compose\") places the instructions of"
" one circuit onto another. They are **inlined**, not wrapped into a single "
"gate, so the result is an ordinary circuit that you can keep decomposing and"
" transpiling.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-3.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"By default a new circuit is returned and both operands are left alone. Pass "
"`inplace=True` to modify the first one instead, and `front=True` to put the "
"operand *before* the existing instructions:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "A narrower circuit can be placed onto a chosen subset of the modes:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A narrow-composed BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-5.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Only another [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") is accepted as the operand, "
"because Qiskit’s own `compose` would inline qubit gates and bypass the check"
" that `append` enforces.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Repeat a circuit {#repeat-a-circuit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[`repeat()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-bosonic-"
"circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.repeat\") repeats a circuit end to "
"end. The repetitions are **flattened**: the result holds the instructions "
"`reps` times in sequence rather than one gate wrapping the circuit. "
"Therefore, the operation counts scale with `reps`, and `decompose` acts on "
"the repeated body instead of removing one repetition.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A repeated BosonicCircuit.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-6.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is the circuit-level way to Trotterize: evolve for a short time, and "
"repeat. See [Synthesize an Evolution gate in bosonic space](bosonic-"
"synthesis#bosonic-synthesis-explanation) for the alternative of choosing a "
"product formula on the gate itself, and why the two are different things "
"that happen to share the word “repetitions”.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Separate steps with barriers {#separate-steps-with-barriers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A **barrier** marks a synchronization point that optimization passes do not "
"fuse gates across. [`barrier()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit.barrier\") places one on all modes, "
"or on the modes you name:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-7.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`repeat(..., insert_barriers=True)` puts one between consecutive "
"repetitions, and none after the last:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A repeated BosonicCircuit with barriers.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-"
"bosons/circuit-8.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Barriers and the encoding {#barriers-and-the-encoding}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An encoding needs several qubits per mode, so the register of modes and the "
"register of qubits differ in size, and a layout relates *whole registers*. A"
" mode therefore has no qubits of its own to narrow a barrier to. During the "
"boson-to-qubit synthesis a barrier is mapped onto **every qubit of each "
"register it touched**, which is correct under any layout:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![A QuantumCircuit showing the expansion of barrier to cover the entire "
"qubit register.](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-bosons/circuit-9.avif)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Read out a bosonic circuit {#read-out-a-bosonic-circuit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"A [`BosonicCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/circuit-"
"bosonic-circuit#qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit "
"\"qiskit_bosons.circuit.BosonicCircuit\") has no `measure` or `measure_all`."
" What a measured bit means depends on the encoding. Under a unary encoding "
"the occupation of a mode is spread over several qubits and has to be read "
"from a pattern of bits, and under a compact one it is a binary number, so a "
"measurement that names a mode would have to know the encoding, which a "
"bosonic circuit deliberately does not. Measure the transpiled "
"[`QuantumCircuit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.QuantumCircuit)"
" instead, and decode the bitstrings with "
"[`LevelEncoding.level_to_bits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-"
"bosons/mappers-level-"
"encoding#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits "
"\"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelEncoding.level_to_bits\") and the offsets of "
"the [`LevelSpec`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-bosons/mappers-"
"level-spec#qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec "
"\"qiskit_bosons.mappers.LevelSpec\") that you lowered with. [Simulate Bose-"
"Hubbard dynamics with a choice of encoding](bose-hubbard#bose-hubbard-"
"getting-started) does this for a complete model.\n"
msgstr ""

